 "text": "Hey! How are things going? Ask open ended questions and try not to sound like a student. Showing genuine interest is what makes a good interview. Perfect! That invites long answer and tells me you' not afraid of quiet moment. That's normal. A quick reminder to keep on track and keep the conversation moving goes a long way. It depends on the person. Some guests like that, others feel caged. A quick pre-call to ask about their preferences is harmless. You got this. Listen more than you speak, and the guest will do most of the talking.",
